WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.480
Least privilege is a practical control for PowerShell automation.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.980
A script should run with the permissions required for the job, not the broadest permissions available to the operator.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:16.000
Unnecessary elevation increases the impact of bugs, bad parameters, compromised hosts, and misuse.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:25.340
Before running a script as administrator, ask which specific resource changes require elevation and whether a narrower role or delegated permission would work.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.520
PowerShell remoting can support strong administrative workflows when it is configured intentionally.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:38.180
Authentication, endpoint configuration, allowed users, network boundaries, logging, and session options all matter.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:45.200
Just Enough Administration is a useful concept because it limits what delegated operators can do through constrained endpoints.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:51.740
Instead of giving broad administrator access, organizations can expose specific commands or functions for specific roles.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.400
Session configuration and role boundaries help separate tasks.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.260
A help desk workflow may need to reset a password but not change domain administrators.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.440
An operations workflow may restart a service but not edit unrelated registry paths.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:11.340
A cloud automation job may need a scoped application permission rather than a global administrator role.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.160
Narrow boundaries turn automation into a controlled capability instead of an all-purpose administrative tunnel.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.620
Auditability is part of the privilege model.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:26.720
Administrative scripts should make it possible to understand what ran, who initiated it, what scope it targeted, and whether it succeeded.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.380
That does not mean logging secrets or excessive personal data.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.880
It means designing automation so important actions are visible, attributable, and reviewable.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:41.460
Secure remoting and privilege design should reduce both accidental damage and ambiguity after an event.
